# The corpus is committed in its reverted state, with __PLANTED_…__ placeholders where the
# credentials go. plant_secrets.py fills them in locally; --revert puts them back.
#
# Nothing here can catch a planted corpus, because planting rewrites the tracked files in place
# rather than creating new ones. Run `python3 plant_secrets.py --check` before committing — that
# is the actual guard, and this file only keeps the incidental output out.

corpus/.chamnan/
.chamnan/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
